{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779397760,"nonce":"9784339JCGJOzehbXIGPse+KuHE=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDBjzHw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/151","origin":"github"},"title":"OAK camera encoder tuning — joint keyframe + resolution measurement campaign for OTH","message":"## Problem\n\nSurfaced from 2026-05-21 deployment debrief: video quality on lossy paths (OTH, Starlink-only, fringe-range WiFi) takes a long time to recover after packet loss because keyframe intervals are configured for bandwidth efficiency. A short loss event garbles many subsequent inter-frames before the next keyframe lets the decoder resync.\n\n**Trade-off**: shorter keyframe interval → faster post-loss recovery → higher bandwidth usage (keyframes are typically several times larger than inter-frames). Optimal point depends on the loss profile of the path.\n\n## Task\n\nMeasurement-driven tuning, in this order:\n\n1. Identify the current keyframe-interval setting in the bizzy OAK launch / encoder config (likely in `bizzyboat_project11/launch/` or wherever the OAK pipeline is configured — needs source-code verification before claiming the location).\n2. Pick 2–3 alternative settings spanning a reasonable range (e.g. 30, 15, 8 frames at the current frame rate).\n3. Capture short OTH or Starlink-only segments at each setting (could fold into the next deployment or use a bench-side lossy-link emulator if available).\n4. Compare:\n   - Visual recovery time after a representative packet loss\n   - Bandwidth used per camera per second\n   - Operator-perceived quality (the qualitative one — does the operator feel like they can drive blind for 10 s vs 30 s)\n5. Pick the setting that balances those for class-day OTH use; document in the camera config with a comment explaining the choice.\n\n## Why now\n\nLake Massabesic surveys go OTH routinely. Operator situational awareness from cameras is one of the key safety nets when the planner doesn't have obstacle avoidance (per the 2026-05-21 collision debrief). A long video-recovery latency turns a 200 ms packet loss into 5+ s of blind operation.\n\n## References\n\n- Source debrief: see [`unh_echoboats_project11#149`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/149) and the 2026-05-21 dev log entry around 17:05 EDT.\n- Roadmap: \"Over-horizon operations capability\" — topic-budget cull intersects this; faster keyframes change which topics dominate the link.\n\n## Anti-scope\n\nThis issue is about the **encoder-side keyframe interval**. Not about the bridge/QoS layer (that's a separate concern). Not about a hardware codec change.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}